  "proposed_label": "bug",
  "proposed_category": "correctness",
  "rationale": "Timer::new computes its deadline using the original runtime handle, then unconditionally pushes the entry onto the current worker runtime registration queue. Resetting a sleep from another runtime can migrate its timer or panic in a current-thread runtime. The introducing patch removed the runtime identity guard; the fix restores the guard and falls back to registration through the original runtime handle.",
